52.25,140.68346354148605 153,139.73301316790798 153.75,138.75 154.5,137.73224073418726 155.25,136.67726406376255 156,135.58225430215302 156.75,134.4439798987516 157.5,133.25870157319775 158.25,132.0220524665192 159,130.72887910686313 159.75,129.37302626111375 160.5,127.94703934553401 161.25,126.44174207655507 162,124.84561866244184 162.75,123.14387691339816 163.5,121.31696392423368 164.25,119.33808316384798 165,117.168742493994 165.75,114.75 166.5,111.98286867171484 167.25,108.67481155659931 168,104.33005198474942 168.75,93.75\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ff0000\" stroke-width=\"1\"></polyline><circle cx=\"93.75\" cy=\"168.75\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#ff0000\" stroke=\"#ff0000\"></circle><polyline points=\"93.75,93.75 101.25,80.75961894323342 108.75,67.76923788646684 116.25,54.77885682970026 123.75,41.78847577293369 131.25,28.7980947161671\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4169e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"></polyline><circle cx=\"131.25\" cy=\"28.7980947161671\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#4169e1\" stroke=\"#4169e1\"></circle><path d=\"M 118.75 93.75 A 25 25 0 0 0 106.25 72.09936490538904\" stroke=\"#4169e1\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\"></path><polygon points=\"106.25,72.09936490538904 112.94615242270663,72.50128869403572 109.94615242270663,77.69744111674235\" fill=\"#4169e1\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"152.75\" y=\"30.25\" width=\"180\" height=\"40\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi style=\"color:#ff0000;\">θ</mi></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"117.75\" y=\"64.25\" width=\"180\" height=\"40\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi style=\"color:#4169e1;\">θ</mi></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"170.75\" y=\"93.75\" width=\"16\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>A</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"124.25\" y=\"93.75\" width=\"16\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>Q</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"126.25\" y=\"6.7980947161671\" width=\"160\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"131.25\" y1=\"93.75\" x2=\"131.25\" y2=\"28.7980947161671\" stroke=\"#4169e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line><line x1=\"168.75\" y1=\"93.75\" x2=\"131.25\" y2=\"28.7980947161671\" stroke=\"#4169e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line></svg><figcaption>Continuity of cosine and sine.</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"!!! proof\n\tLet ``A``, ``P`` and ``Q`` be the points as shown in the figure.\n\n\tSince the length of chord ``AP`` is less than the length of arc ``AP``, we have\n\t```math\n\t\\sin^2\\theta+\\left(1-\\cos\\theta\\right)^2<\\theta^2\\,.\n\t```\n\tSquaring yields positive values and the square root is an increasing function, so\n\t```math\n\t0\\le\\left|\\sin\\theta\\right|<\\left|\\theta\\right|\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad 0\\le\\left|1-\\cos\\theta\\right|<\\left|\\theta\\right|\\,.\n\t```\n\tUsing the squeeze theorem, we find\n\t```math\n\t0\\le\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\left|\\sin\\theta\\right|<\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\left|\\theta\\right|=0\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad 0\\le\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\left|1-\\cos\\theta\\right|<\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\left|\\theta\\right|=0\\,.\n\t```\n\tThus,\n\t```math\n\t\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\sin\\theta = 0=\\sin0\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\cos\\theta = 1=\\cos0\n\t```\n\tand sine and cosine are continuous at ``\\theta=0``.\n\n\tTo prove the continuity at another point, we use the addition formulas and the rules to evaluate limits:\n\t```math\n\t\\lim_{\\theta\\to \\theta_0}\\sin\\theta=\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\sin(\\theta_0+\\phi)=\\sin\\theta_0\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\cos\\phi+\\cos\\theta_0\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\sin\\phi=\\sin\\theta_0\n\t```\n\tand\n\t```math\n\t\\lim_{\\theta\\to \\theta_0}\\cos\\theta=\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\cos(\\theta_0+\\phi)=\\cos\\theta_0\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\cos\\phi-\\sin\\theta_0\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\sin\\phi=\\cos\\theta_0\\,.\n\t```\n\nThe graph of the function ``\\displaystyle\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\theta}`` is shown in the next figure. Although it is not defined at ``\\theta=0``, this function appears to have limit ``1`` as ``\\theta`` approaches ``0``.","output":"","result":"!!! proof\n\tLet ``A``, ``P`` and ``Q`` be the points as shown in the figure.\n\n\tSince the length of chord ``AP`` is less than the length of arc ``AP``, we have\n\t```math\n\t\\sin^2\\theta+\\left(1-\\cos\\theta\\right)^2<\\theta^2\\,.\n\t```\n\tSquaring yields positive values and the square root is an increasing function, so\n\t```math\n\t0\\le\\left|\\sin\\theta\\right|<\\left|\\theta\\right|\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad 0\\le\\left|1-\\cos\\theta\\right|<\\left|\\theta\\right|\\,.\n\t```\n\tUsing the squeeze theorem, we find\n\t```math\n\t0\\le\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\left|\\sin\\theta\\right|<\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\left|\\theta\\right|=0\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad 0\\le\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\left|1-\\cos\\theta\\right|<\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\left|\\theta\\right|=0\\,.\n\t```\n\tThus,\n\t```math\n\t\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\sin\\theta = 0=\\sin0\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\lim_{\\theta\\to 0}\\cos\\theta = 1=\\cos0\n\t```\n\tand sine and cosine are continuous at ``\\theta=0``.\n\n\tTo prove the continuity at another point, we use the addition formulas and the rules to evaluate limits:\n\t```math\n\t\\lim_{\\theta\\to \\theta_0}\\sin\\theta=\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\sin(\\theta_0+\\phi)=\\sin\\theta_0\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\cos\\phi+\\cos\\theta_0\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\sin\\phi=\\sin\\theta_0\n\t```\n\tand\n\t```math\n\t\\lim_{\\theta\\to \\theta_0}\\cos\\theta=\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\cos(\\theta_0+\\phi)=\\cos\\theta_0\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\cos\\phi-\\sin\\theta_0\\lim_{\\phi\\to0}\\sin\\phi=\\cos\\theta_0\\,.\n\t```\n\nThe graph of the function ``\\displaystyle\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\theta}`` is shown in the next figure. Although it is not defined at ``\\theta=0``, this function appears to have limit ``1`` as ``\\theta`` approaches ``0``.","resultHTML":"<aside class=\"markdown-admonition markdown-admonition-proof\"><div class=\"markdown-admonition-title\">Proof</div><div class=\"markdown-admonition-body\"><p>Let <math><mi>A</mi></math>, <math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> be the points as shown in the figure.</p>\n<p>Since the length of chord <math><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></math> is less than the length of arc <math><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></math>, we have</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mi>.</mi></mrow></math>\n<p>Squaring yields positive values and the square root is an increasing function, so</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mi>.</mi></mrow></math>\n<p>Using the squeeze theorem, we find</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mi>.</mi></mrow></math>\n<p>Thus,</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>and sine and cosine are continuous at <math><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.</p>\n<p>To prove the continuity at another point, we use the addition formulas and the rules to evaluate limits:</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></math>\n<p>and</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mi>.</mi></mrow></math></div></aside>\n<p>The graph of the function <math><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></math> is shown in the next figure. Although it is not defined at <math><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, this function appears to have limit <math><mn>1</mn></math> as <math><mi>θ</mi></math> approaches <math><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 40;\nconst xmid = 7 * scale;\nconst ymid = 1.5 * scale;\n\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n    width: 14 * scale,\n    height: 2.2 * scale+10,\n    caption: \"\\\\(\\\\lim_{θ → 0} \\\\frac{\\\\sin(θ)}{θ} = 1\\\\)\",\n});\n\nfigure.axes({\n    origin: [xmid, ymid],\n    scale,\n    x: {\n        ticks: [\n            { value: -2 * Math.PI, label: String.raw`-2\\pi`, length: 3 },\n            { value: -Math.PI, label: String.raw`-\\pi`, length: 2 },\n            { value: -Math.PI / 2, label: String.raw`-\\frac{\\pi}{2}`, length: 2 },\n            { value: Math.PI / 2, label: String.raw`\\frac{\\pi}{2}`, length: 2 },\n            { value: Math.PI, label: String.raw`\\pi`, length: 1 },\n            { value: 2 * Math.PI, label: String.raw`2\\pi`, length: 2 },\n        ],\n    },\n    y: { ticks: [1] },\n});\n\nfigure.label(\"O\", {\n    x: xmid - 16,\n    y: ymid,\n    width: 14,\n    height: 18,\n    latex: true,\n});\n\nconst sinc = (x) => Math.sin(x) / x;\n\nfigure.plot(sinc, {\n    domain: [-7, -0.01],\n    samples: 700,\n    stroke: \"#ff0000\",\n    width: 1,\n});\nfigure.plot(sinc, {\n    domain: [0.01, 7],\n    samples: 700,\n    stroke: \"#ff0000\",\n    width: 1,\n});\n\nfigure.point(0, 1, {\n    radius: 3,\n    fill: \"#ffffff\",\n    stroke: \"#ff0000\",\n});\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"xy−2π−π−π2π2π2π1Olimθ→0⁡sin⁡(θ)θ=1","resultHTML":"<figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"560\" height=\"98\" viewBox=\"0 0 560 98\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"560\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><line x1=\"280\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><polygon points=\"560,60 553,56 553,64\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><polygon points=\"280,0 276,7 284,7\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"546\" y=\"30\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"288\" y=\"-2\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"28.67258771281655\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"28.67258771281655\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"7.672587712816551\" y=\"68\" width=\"42\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"154.33629385640828\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"154.33629385640828\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"140.33629385640828\" y=\"68\" width=\"28\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"217.16814692820412\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"217.16814692820412\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"203.16814692820412\" y=\"68\" width=\"28\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"342.8318530717959\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"342.8318530717959\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"328.8318530717959\" y=\"68\" width=\"28\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"405.66370614359175\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"405.66370614359175\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"398.66370614359175\" y=\"68\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>π</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"531.3274122871835\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"531.3274122871835\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"517.3274122871835\" y=\"68\" width=\"28\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"276\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"284\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"256\" y=\"8\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"264\" y=\"60\" width=\"14\" height=\"18\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>O</mi></math></div></foreignObject><polyline points=\"0,56.24579086446406 0.39999999999997726,56.28374905425516 0.7999999999999545,56.32218816117516 1.1999999999999886,56.36110587260154 1.6000000000000227,56.40049982573761 2,56.440367607694824 2.3999999999999773,56.48070675557937 2.8000000000000114,56.52151475658313 3.1999999999999886,56.562789048079026 3.6000000000000227,56.60452701772071 4,56.64672600354667 4.400000000000034,56.68938329408856 4.800000000000011,56.73249612848405 5.199999999999989,56.77606169659394 5.599999999999966,56.820077139123605 6,56.86453954774884 6.399999999999977,56.90944596524602 6.800000000000011,56.954793385626594 7.199999999999989,57.00057875427594 7.600000000000023,57.046798968096496 8,57.09345087565524 8.399999999999977,57.14053127733555 8.800000000000011,57.18803692549322 9.200000000000045,57.23596452461694 9.600000000000023,57.28431073149296 10,57.33307215537412 10.399999999999977,57.3822453581531 10.799999999999955,57.431826854539985 11.199999999999989,57.48181311224407 11.600000000000023,57.53220055215989 12,57.58298554855762 12.399999999999977,57.63416442927755 12.800000000000011,57.68573347592886 13.199999999999989,57.73768892409269 13.600000000000023,57.79002696352922 14,57.842743738389174 14.400000000000034,57.895835347429305 14.800000000000011,57.9492978442322 15.199999999999989,58.00312723743014 15.599999999999966,58.057319490933196 16,58.111870524161