01 220.79999999999998,97.60000000000002 221.20000000000002,97.39999999999998 221.59999999999997,97.20000000000002 222,97 222.39999999999998,96.8 222.79999999999998,96.6 223.2,96.4 223.6,96.20000000000002 224,96.00000000000001 224.4,95.79999999999998 224.8,95.6 225.2,95.39999999999999 225.6,95.19999999999999 226,95 226.4,94.80000000000001 226.8,94.60000000000001 227.2,94.4 227.59999999999997,94.20000000000002 228,93.99999999999999 228.4,93.79999999999998 228.79999999999998,93.6 229.20000000000002,93.4 229.60000000000002,93.2 230,93 230.39999999999998,92.80000000000001 230.79999999999998,92.60000000000002 231.20000000000002,92.39999999999998 231.6,92.19999999999999 232,92 232.40000000000003,91.8 232.8,91.6 233.2,91.4 233.6,91.20000000000002 234,91.00000000000001 234.4,90.79999999999998 234.8,90.6 235.2,90.39999999999999 235.6,90.19999999999999 236,90 236.4,89.80000000000001 236.8,89.60000000000001 237.2,89.4 237.59999999999997,89.20000000000002 238,88.99999999999999 238.4,88.79999999999998 238.79999999999998,88.6 239.20000000000002,88.4 239.60000000000002,88.2 240,88\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ff0000\" stroke-width=\"1\"></polyline><foreignObject x=\"70\" y=\"0\" width=\"180\" height=\"40\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi style=\"color:#4169e1;\">y</mi><mo style=\"color:#4169e1;\">=</mo><mi style=\"color:#4169e1;\">f</mi><mrow style=\"color:#4169e1;\"><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"170\" y=\"120\" width=\"180\" height=\"40\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi style=\"color:#ff0000;\">x</mi><mo style=\"color:#ff0000;\">=</mo><msup style=\"color:#ff0000;\"><mi>f</mi><mrow class=\"tml-lrg-pad\"><mo stretchy=\"false\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow style=\"color:#ff0000;\"><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"60\" y=\"80\" width=\"42\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"140\" y=\"140\" width=\"42\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></math></div></foreignObject></svg><figcaption>Tangents to the graphs of <math><mi>f</mi></math> and <math><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow class=\"tml-lrg-pad\"><mo stretchy=\"false\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"!!! example\n\n\tShow that ``f\\left(x\\right)=x^3+x`` is bijective on the whole real line, and, nothing that ``f\\left(2\\right)=10``, find ``\\left(f^{-1}\\right)^\\prime\\left(10\\right)``.\n\n\tSince ``f^\\prime\\left(x\\right)=3x^2+1>0`` for all real numbers ``x``, ``f`` is increasing and therefore bijective and invertible. If ``y=f^{-1}\\left(x\\right)``, then\n\t```math\n\t\\begin{aligned}\n\tx=f\\left(y\\right)=y^3+y &\\implies 1=(3y^2+1)y^\\prime\\\\\n\t&\\implies y^\\prime=\\frac{1}{3y^2+1}\\,.\n\t\\end{aligned}\n\t```\n\tNow ``x=f\\left(2\\right)=10`` implies ``y=f^{-1}\\left(10\\right)=2``. Thus,\n\t```math\n\t\\left(f^{-1}\\right)^\\prime\\left(10\\right)=\\left.\\frac{1}{3y^2+1}\\right|_{y=2}=\\frac{1}{13}\\,.\n\t```","output":"","result":"!!! example\n\n\tShow that ``f\\left(x\\right)=x^3+x`` is bijective on the whole real line, and, nothing that ``f\\left(2\\right)=10``, find ``\\left(f^{-1}\\right)^\\prime\\left(10\\right)``.\n\n\tSince ``f^\\prime\\left(x\\right)=3x^2+1>0`` for all real numbers ``x``, ``f`` is increasing and therefore bijective and invertible. If ``y=f^{-1}\\left(x\\right)``, then\n\t```math\n\t\\begin{aligned}\n\tx=f\\left(y\\right)=y^3+y &\\implies 1=(3y^2+1)y^\\prime\\\\\n\t&\\implies y^\\prime=\\frac{1}{3y^2+1}\\,.\n\t\\end{aligned}\n\t```\n\tNow ``x=f\\left(2\\right)=10`` implies ``y=f^{-1}\\left(10\\right)=2``. Thus,\n\t```math\n\t\\left(f^{-1}\\right)^\\prime\\left(10\\right)=\\left.\\frac{1}{3y^2+1}\\right|_{y=2}=\\frac{1}{13}\\,.\n\t```","resultHTML":"<aside class=\"markdown-admonition markdown-admonition-example\"><div class=\"markdown-admonition-title\">Example</div><div class=\"markdown-admonition-body\"><p>Show that <math><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn class=\"tml-sml-pad\">3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> is bijective on the whole real line, and, nothing that <math><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math>, find <math><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow class=\"tml-lrg-pad\"><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo class=\"tml-prime\">′</mo></msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>.</p>\n<p>Since <math><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn class=\"tml-sml-pad\">2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> for all real numbers <math><mi>x</mi></math>, <math><mi>f</mi></math> is increasing and therefore bijective and invertible. If <math><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow class=\"tml-lrg-pad\"><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>, then</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" class=\"tml-jot\"><mtr><mtd class=\"tml-right\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn class=\"tml-sml-pad\">3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class=\"tml-left\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2778em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟹</mo><mspace width=\"0.2778em\"></mspace><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn class=\"tml-sml-pad\">2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-sml-pad\">′</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class=\"tml-right\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class=\"tml-left\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2778em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟹</mo><mspace width=\"0.2778em\"></mspace><msup><mi>y</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-sml-pad\">′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn class=\"tml-sml-pad\">2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mi>.</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>\n<p>Now <math><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math> implies <math><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow class=\"tml-lrg-pad\"><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. Thus,</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow class=\"tml-lrg-pad\"><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo class=\"tml-prime\">′</mo></msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\"></mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn class=\"tml-sml-pad\">2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>13</mn></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mi>.</mi></mrow></math></div></aside>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"## The Mean-Value Theorem\n\nIf you set out in a car at 1:00 p.m. and arrive in a town 150 km away from your starting point at 3:00 p.m., then you have travelled at an average speed of ``\\frac{150}{2}=75`` km/h. Although you may not have travelled at constant speed, you must have been going 75 km/h at at least one instant during your journey, for if your speed was always less than 75 km/h you would have gone less than 150 km in 2 h, and if your speed was always more than 75 km/h, you would have gone more than 150 km in 2 h. In order to get from a value less than 75 km/h to a value greater than 75 km/h, your speed, which is a continuous function of time, must pass through the value 75 km/h at some intermediate time.\n\nThe conclusion that the average speed over a time interval must be equal to the instantaneous speed at some time in that interval is an instance of an important mathematical principle. In geometric terms it says that if ``A`` and ``B`` are two points on a smooth curve, then there is at least one point ``C`` on the curve between ``A`` and ``B`` where the tangent line is parallel to the chord line ``AB``.","output":"","result":"## The Mean-Value Theorem\n\nIf you set out in a car at 1:00 p.m. and arrive in a town 150 km away from your starting point at 3:00 p.m., then you have travelled at an average speed of ``\\frac{150}{2}=75`` km/h. Although you may not have travelled at constant speed, you must have been going 75 km/h at at least one instant during your journey, for if your speed was always less than 75 km/h you would have gone less than 150 km in 2 h, and if your speed was always more than 75 km/h, you would have gone more than 150 km in 2 h. In order to get from a value less than 75 km/h to a value greater than 75 km/h, your speed, which is a continuous function of time, must pass through the value 75 km/h at some intermediate time.\n\nThe conclusion that the average speed over a time interval must be equal to the instantaneous speed at some time in that interval is an instance of an important mathematical principle. In geometric terms it says that if ``A`` and ``B`` are two points on a smooth curve, then there is at least one point ``C`` on the curve between ``A`` and ``B`` where the tangent line is parallel to the chord line ``AB``.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-y2ubvb-1547-7ueozw-the-mean-value-theorem\">The Mean-Value Theorem</h2>\n<p>If you set out in a car at 1:00 p.m. and arrive in a town 150 km away from your starting point at 3:00 p.m., then you have travelled at an average speed of <math><mrow><mfrac><mn>150</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn></mrow></math> km/h. Although you may not have travelled at constant speed, you must have been going 75 km/h at at least one instant during your journey, for if your speed was always less than 75 km/h you would have gone less than 150 km in 2 h, and if your speed was always more than 75 km/h, you would have gone more than 150 km in 2 h. In order to get from a value less than 75 km/h to a value greater than 75 km/h, your speed, which is a continuous function of time, must pass through the value 75 km/h at some intermediate time.</p>\n<p>The conclusion that the average speed over a time interval must be equal to the instantaneous speed at some time in that interval is an instance of an important mathematical principle. In geometric terms it says that if <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> are two points on a smooth curve, then there is at least one point <math><mi>C</mi></math> on the curve between <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> where the tangent line is parallel to the chord line <math><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 40;\nconst xmid = scale;\nconst ymid = 5 * scale;\nconst fontX = 14;\nconst fontY = 22\n\nconst f = (x) => -0.5 * (x - 2) ** 2 + 4;\nconst c = 1.5;\nconst fc = f(c);\nconst a = -0.5;\nconst fa = f(a);\nconst b = 3.5;\nconst fb = f(b);\n\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n    width: 6 * scale,\n    height: 5.5 * scale+10,\n    caption: \"There is a point C on the curve where the tangent (green) is parallel to the chord AB (blue).\",\n});\n\nfigure.axes({\n    origin: [xmid, ymid],\n    scale,\n    x: {\n        ticks: [\n            { value: a, label: \"a\", length: 1 },\n            { value: b, label: \"b\", length: 1 },\n            { value: c, label: \"c\", length: 1 },\n        ],\n    },\n    y: { ticks: [] },\n});\n\nfigure.label(\"O\", {\n    x: xmid - 16,\n    y: ymid,\n    width: fontX,\n    height: fontY,\n    latex: true,\n});\n\nfigure.plot(f, {\n    domain: [-1, 5.5],\n    samples: 651,\n    stroke: \"#ff0000\",\n    width: 1,\n});\nfor (const x of [a, b, c]) {\n    figure.point(x, f(x), { radius: 3, fill: \"#ff0000\", stroke: \"#ff0000\" });\n}\n\nconst tangentSlope = -(c - 2);\nfigure.plot((x) => tangentSlope * (x - c) + fc, {\n    domain: [-1, 5.5],\n    samples: 651,\n    stroke: \"#008000\",\n    width: 1,\n});\n\nfigure.plot((x) => tangentSlope * (x - a) + fa, {\n    domain: [a, b],\n    samples: 401,\n    stroke: \"#4169e1\",\n    width: 1,\n});\n\nfunction dashedGuide(x, y) {\n    figure.line()\n        .x1(xmid + x * scale).y1(ymid - y * scale)\n        .x2(xmid + x * scale).y2(ymid)\n        .stroke(\"#000000\")\n        .setAttribute(\"stroke-dasharray\", \"3\");\n}\n\ndashedGuide(a, fa);\ndashedGuide(b, fb);\ndashedGuide(c, fc);\n\nfigure.label(\"y = f(x)\", {\n    x: xmid + 3 * scale,\n    y: ymid - 4 * scale,\n    width: 4 * fontX,\n    height: fontY,\n    latex: true,\n});\n\nfigure.label(\"A\", {\n    x: xmid + a * scale - 0.6 * fontX,\n    y: ymid - fa * scale - 1.25 * fontY,\n    width: fontX,\n    height: fontY,\n    latex: true,\n});\nfigure.label(\"B\", {\n    x: xmid + b * scale - 0.5 * fontX,\n    y: ymid - fb * scale - 1.25 * fontY,\n    width: fontX,\n    height: fontY,\n    latex: true,\n});\nfigure.label(\"C\", {\n    x: xmid + c * scale - 0.5 * fontX,\n    y: ymid - fc * scale - 1.25 * fontY,\n    width: fontX,\n    height: fontY,\n    latex: true,\n});\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"xyabcOy=f(x)ABCThere is a point C on the curve where the tangent (green) is parallel to the chord AB (blue).","resultHTML":"<figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"240\" height=\"230\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 230\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><polygon points=\"240,200 233,196 233,204\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><polygon points=\"40,0 36,7 44,7\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"226\" y=\"170\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"48\" y=\"-2\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"204\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"13\" y=\"208\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"180\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"204\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"173\" y=\"208\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>b</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"204\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"93\" y=\"208\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"24\" y=\"200\" width=\"14\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>O</mi></math></div></foreignObject><polyline points=\"0,220 0.3999999999999986,218.80200000000002 0.7999999999999972,217.608 1.2000000000000028,216.41799999999995 1.6000000000000014,215.232 2,214.05 2.4000000000000057,212.87199999999999 2.8000000000000043,211.69799999999995 3.1999999999999957,210.52799999999996 3.6000000000000014,209.36200000000002 4,208.2 4.399999999999999,207.042 4.799999999999997,205.88799999999998 5.200000000000003,204.738 5.600000000000001,203.59199999999998 6,202.45000000000002 6.399999999999999,201.312 6.80000000